WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.430
Apple Sales International, one
of Apple's Irish subsidiaries.

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.510
In 2003, its effective
tax rate was 1 per cent.

3
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:13.190
By 2014, it was 0.005 per cent.

4
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.730
Ireland's standard corporation
tax rate is 12.5 per cent.

5
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.610
How is that possible?

6
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.210
Did the company break Irish criminal law?

7
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.690
Did it make no profit?

8
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:25.010
And who loses?

9
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.590
In this mission, you'll separate
tax avoidance from tax evasion,

10
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.010
and estimate how much profit
is shifted to low-tax places.

11
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.850
Then you'll follow the case
to the EU's Court of Justice,

12
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.870
and on to a global minimum tax.

13
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:44.610
Your mission: explain how the
subsidiary paid tax at 0.005 per cent,

14
00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.290
and who loses.
